{
 "brief": "Israeli occupation forces demolished 12 commercial warehouses at the entrance to Anaza village south of Jenin on Tuesday morning, Shehab Wire reported. The structures stood near the village's main approach and served as retail storage facilities.\n\nThe demolition proceeded despite ongoing court proceedings in Israeli courts examining the case. No final judicial ruling had been issued on the matter at the time of the operation, according to the report. The timing of the demolition while legal review remained pending raised questions about the coordination between military and judicial authorities overseeing settlement-area operations.",
